    "result_text": "The full suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct level-computation rule with a points system, then derived the level from those points.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** (the single place membership was computed):\n- Added `membershipPoints(Owner)` \u2014 starts at 0; **+2** email present, **+1** `namesakeCount == 0`, **+2** household of 3+ (`householdSize >= 3`), **+3** tenure over 365 days.\n- Rewrote `membershipLevel(Owner)` to derive from `membershipPoints`: 1 (0\u20131), 2 (2\u20133), 3 (4\u20135), 4 (6+) \u2014 no longer duplicating the factor logic.\n- Extracted a private `hasEmail(Owner)` helper, now reused by both `membershipPoints` and `contactPreference` instead of the duplicated inline email check.\n- Added the `membershipPoints` MapStruct `@Mapping` so both fields are returned.\n\n**`openapi.yml`**: added the `membershipPoints` schema property (the DTO field is generated from this) and updated the `membershipLevel` description to reflect the new derivation.\n\n`AuditOwnerCreated` continues to log `membershipLevel` unchanged \u2014 it reuses the mapper, so it now reflects the new mapping automatically.\n\nTests: the new `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsPointsAndLevel` (email + no namesake \u2192 3 points \u2192 level 2) passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
