    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`, traced from `owners.POST.yml` and each function class. Everything runs inside one write transaction (`govern: [ transaction ]` on every step), committed once at the end.\n\n**Gate (before any step)**\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. Caller must have role `OWNER_ADMIN` or the whole endpoint is rejected.\n\n**Pipeline steps, in order**\n\n1. **NormalizeOwnerAddress** *(side-effect)* \u2014 reads the `@RequestBody` **once**, normalizes the address (`OwnerAddresses.normalize`), and republishes the request as a variable for all later steps. Every later address use sees this normalized form.\n2. **ValidateRequiredOwnerFields** *(validation)* \u2014 rejects if any of `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` is null/blank \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException`. Address checked is the normalized one.\n3. **ValidateOwnerPostcode** *(validation)* \u2014 postcode optional; if present must be exactly 4 digits and fall within the pinned range for the city's region (`Locality.postcodeAllowedForCity`) \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (400).\n4. **RejectFutureRegistrationDate** *(validation)* \u2014 if a registration date was supplied and is after the server's current date \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400). Checks the raw supplied date before any roll-forward.\n5. **ResolveOwnerRegistrationDate** *(side-effect)* \u2014 computes the effective registration date (supplied, else today), rolls weekends forward to the next business day (`BusinessDays.rollForward`), and publishes it as a `LocalDate` variable.\n6. **RejectDailyOwnerLimit** *(validation)* \u2014 if \u2265 100 owners already registered on that business day \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (429).\n7. **RejectFullOwnerCity** *(validation)* \u2014 if the city already holds \u2265 50 owners (counted case-insensitively) \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n8. **NormalizeOwnerTelephone** *(side-effect)* \u2014 normalizes telephone to E.164 (`OwnerTelephones.toE164`), stored back on the request; may throw `InvalidTelephoneException`.\n9. **NormalizeOwnerEmail** *(validation + side-effect)* \u2014 email optional; if blank/null it's cleared to null; if present it's lower-cased/normalized and must be syntactically valid \u2192 else `InvalidEmailException` (400).\n10. **RejectDisposableOwnerEmail** *(validation)* \u2014 if the (normalized) email's domain is a disposable-email provider \u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException` (400). No-op when email absent.\n11. **RejectDuplicateOwnerHousehold** *(validation)* \u2014 if an existing owner shares the same last name + postcode (household key) \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerException` (409). Bypassed when the request sets `sharesHousehold = true`.\n12. **BuildOwner** *(side-effect)* \u2014 maps the request DTO to an `Owner` entity (`OwnerMapper.toOwner`), published for the remaining steps.\n13. **AssignOwnerNamesakeCount** *(side-effect)* \u2014 counts existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive) and stamps `namesakeCount` on the owner.\n14. **ApplyOwnerRegistrationDate** *(side-effect)* \u2014 stamps the resolved business-day registration date onto the owner, overwriting whatever raw date the request carried.\n15. **AssignOwnerCustomerCode** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode; hash = first 8 upper-hex chars of SHA-256 over normalized telephone + last name).\n16. **AssignOwnerHousehold** *(side-effect)* \u2014 stamps `householdId`, derived deterministically from last name + postcode.\n17. **AssignOwnerHouseholdSize** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `householdSize` = 1 + existing members sharing last name + postcode (counts this new owner).\n18. **AssignOwnerBulkSignupWarning** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` when more than 80 owners were already registered on that business day.\n19. **AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate** *(side-effect)* \u2014 if not a declared household member (`sharesHousehold`), and an existing owner shares last name + postcode but has a *different* telephone, sets `possibleDuplicateOf` to the lowest matching owner id. No-op when no postcode.\n20. **SaveOwner** *(side-effect)* \u2014 persists the owner via `OwnerRepository.save` (assigns its id).\n21. **AuditOwnerCreated** *(side-effect)* \u2014 logs to the `AUDIT` logger: id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel.\n22. **RespondWithOwnerCreated** *(side-effect / response)* \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto` and returns **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n**Notes on ordering rationale (from the code):**\n- Validations run before persistence-shaping steps, and body-reading happens exactly once (step 1) because the HTTP body may only be bound once.\n- The duplicate-household *rejection* (11) precedes the soft *possible-duplicate* flag (19); both compare against owners existing before this create.\n- The daily-limit reject (6) and bulk-signup warning (18) count against the same resolved business day.\n- Any escalation thrown maps to a handler under `officefloor/escalation/\u2026` (e.g. `MissingOwnerFieldsException`, `InvalidPostcodeException`, `DuplicateOwnerException`, etc.); the transaction commits only if all steps succeed."
